+The reporting extension supplements the earlier frozen and donor inventory without changing the definition of its original assessment protocols.
+
+Selected saved-prediction verification conducted on 25 November 2026 examines numerical consistency using the retained fitted-model outputs.
+
+For the REASSEMBLE F2 investigation, the verification examines prediction identities, branch-score parity within the available records, fold assignments, fitted coefficients, and the corresponding ranking metrics.
+
+For ViFailback, the verification examines the available saved assessment vectors, metric consistency, and completion records associated with the extended reporting boundary.
+
+These checks do not reproduce the original neural fitting procedures or establish independent experimental replication.
+
+The evidence records document source paths, hashes, assessment identities, metric definitions, and the boundaries of the performed verification.
+
+The literature extraction records separately connect external scientific claims to their bibliographic sources and relevant publication passages.
+
+Appendix~\ref{app:reproducibility} provides the reproducibility documentation, while the evidence register and Appendix~\ref{app:chronology} establish the associated source provenance and research chronology.
